    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Question\n\nHi, thanks for making this!\r\n\r\nI've been trying `mini.clue` after using `which-key`, and missing one thing: if I have a mapping like\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>w', '<C-w>', { desc = '+Window' })\r\n```\r\n\r\nI can't seem to get the `miniclue.gen_clues.windows()` clues to pop up when I use the `<leader>w` mapping. It shows `<C-w>` in my status line, but the clues only show up when I actually hit `<C-w>`. In which-key I was able to do this using the [proxy setting](https://github.com/folke/which-key.nvim/blob/904308e6885bbb7b60714c80ab3daf0c071c1492/doc/which-key.nvim.txt#L316). Is there a way to make this work?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.clue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi, thanks for making this!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've been trying <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.clue</code> after using <code class=\"notranslate\">which-key</code>, and missing one thing: if I have a mapping like</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;leader&gt;w', '&lt;C-w&gt;', { desc = '+Window' })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;w<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;C-w&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>+Window<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I can't seem to get the <code class=\"notranslate\">miniclue.gen_clues.windows()</code> clues to pop up when I use the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;leader&gt;w</code> mapping. It shows <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-w&gt;</code> in my status line, but the clues only show up when I actually hit <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-w&gt;</code>. In which-key I was able to do this using the <a href=\"https://github.com/folke/which-key.nvim/blob/904308e6885bbb7b60714c80ab3daf0c071c1492/doc/which-key.nvim.txt#L316\">proxy setting</a>. Is there a way to make this work?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.clue\nQuestion\nHi, thanks for making this!\nI've been trying mini.clue after using which-key, and missing one thing: if I have a mapping like\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>w', '<C-w>', { desc = '+Window' })\nI can't seem to get the miniclue.gen_clues.windows() clues to pop up when I use the <leader>w mapping. It shows <C-w> in my status line, but the clues only show up when I actually hit <C-w>. In which-key I was able to do this using the proxy setting. Is there a way to make this work?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
