                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "I switched to use\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>w', function()\r\n  vim.api.nvim_input '<C-w>'\r\nend, { desc = '+Window' })\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd this seems to work better in that\r\n- The special mini.clues setup isn't required\r\n- With the previous setup above, I realized I couldn't actually use some bindings, for example instead of \"Show diagnostics under cursor\" for \\<C-w\\>d (`CTRL-W_d-default`), I could only use \"Split + jump to definition\" with \\<leader\\>wd. I don't think this had anything to do with mini.clue\r\n\r\nSome caveats though\r\n- mini.clue no longer immediately pops up the \\<C-w\\> clues when typing \\<leader\\> then waiting then \"w\". Because it's pressing a whole new key sequence, the mini.clue delay re-applies. Not a big deal for me though\r\n- Not sure how binding under \\<leader\\>w would work now, I'd probably just bind under \\<C-w\\>",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I switched to use</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;leader&gt;w', function()\n  vim.api.nvim_input '&lt;C-w&gt;'\nend, { desc = '+Window' })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;leader&gt;w<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_input</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;C-w&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>+Window<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">And this seems to work better in that</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The special mini.clues setup isn't required</li>\n<li>With the previous setup above, I realized I couldn't actually use some bindings, for example instead of \"Show diagnostics under cursor\" for &lt;C-w&gt;d (<code class=\"notranslate\">CTRL-W_d-default</code>), I could only use \"Split + jump to definition\" with &lt;leader&gt;wd. I don't think this had anything to do with mini.clue</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Some caveats though</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>mini.clue no longer immediately pops up the &lt;C-w&gt; clues when typing &lt;leader&gt; then waiting then \"w\". Because it's pressing a whole new key sequence, the mini.clue delay re-applies. Not a big deal for me though</li>\n<li>Not sure how binding under &lt;leader&gt;w would work now, I'd probably just bind under &lt;C-w&gt;</li>\n</ul>",
                    "bodyText": "I switched to use\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>w', function()\n  vim.api.nvim_input '<C-w>'\nend, { desc = '+Window' })\nAnd this seems to work better in that\n\nThe special mini.clues setup isn't required\nWith the previous setup above, I realized I couldn't actually use some bindings, for example instead of \"Show diagnostics under cursor\" for <C-w>d (CTRL-W_d-default), I could only use \"Split + jump to definition\" with <leader>wd. I don't think this had anything to do with mini.clue\n\nSome caveats though\n\nmini.clue no longer immediately pops up the <C-w> clues when typing <leader> then waiting then \"w\". Because it's pressing a whole new key sequence, the mini.clue delay re-applies. Not a big deal for me though\nNot sure how binding under <leader>w would work now, I'd probably just bind under <C-w>",
